scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: the-expanse
run_id: 1
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 15
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase addressed distinguishing NotFound from parse/permission errors
    in from_file_or_default. The config tests exercise loading but never assert that
    parse errors or permission errors propagate rather than falling back to defaults.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented sanitized Display messages: 'Internal(String) displays\
    \ \"An internal error occurred\", not the inner string.' Reviewer verified CWE-209\
    \ sanitization. However, the Io(#[error(transparent)]) variant still forwards\
    \ full OS details \u2014 the fix is incomplete but the issue was actively addressed."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #7: 'with_tenant() and with_token() bypass validation\
    \ \u2014 validated variants are separate methods... Nothing prevents callers from\
    \ using the unvalidated path, making header injection prevention opt-in rather\
    \ than default-safe.' TEA also wrote header injection tests, and dev implemented\
    \ CR/LF/null validation, but neither enforced TenantId from axiathon-core at the\
    \ type level."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "Reviewer incorrectly marked as '[VERIFIED] Workspace dependency declarations\
    \ correct \u2014 all deps use { workspace = true }'. The ground truth confirms\
    \ 6 deps use direct version strings. False verification."
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #4: 'RawConfig silently ignores unknown fields \u2014\
    \ no #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]... a token field is silently ignored rather\
    \ than rejected. The test asserts has_token() is false, but the real security\
    \ posture should warn the user that they're putting secrets in a config file,\
    \ not silently eat them.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'TEA wrote the test containing the vacuous assertion (assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...)), and neither Dev nor Reviewer flagged the logical tautology. Reviewer
    flagged a different vacuous test (exit_code_success_is_zero, finding #8) but missed
    this one.'
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote the test with 'let _ = config;' and zero assertions. No phase
    flagged that the test only checks non-panic behavior without verifying any return
    values.
